GnomeAI-RS for Debian
=====================

The package itself must be installed by an administrator, but both applications
run as the desktop user afterward. Runtime data and API keys are stored with
owner-only permissions under:

  ${XDG_STATE_HOME:-$HOME/.local/state}/gnomeai-rs

No application command should be launched with sudo.

Applications
------------

The desktop menu contains:

* GnomeAI-RS Agent — terminal coding agent with /workspace, /provider,
  /websearch and installable SKILL.md packages. The transcript supports
  mouse-wheel and keyboard scrolling.
  Hold the left mouse button while using the wheel to extend a selection
  beyond the viewport; releasing the button copies the selection.
* GnomeAI-RS WebTool — local browser interface at http://127.0.0.1:8787.

Equivalent commands:

  gnomeai-rs /path/to/workspace
  gnomeai-webtool

Execution modes
---------------

`normal` is the default: commands may use normal user-level host access after
an approval. `full-access` skips approval prompts, and `read-only` blocks
mutations. These modes never grant root privileges; do not launch the agent
with sudo. Strict upload parsers and generated-document jobs continue to use
their own fail-closed Landlock/seccomp sandbox.

Skills
------

The Agent, WebTool and WhatsApp share the native Rust skill manager. Managed
packages are installed under:

  ${XDG_DATA_HOME:-$HOME/.local/share}/gnomeai-rs/skills

The Agent commands are `/skills` and
`/skill use|inspect|install|update|verify|remove`. WebTool exposes the manager
in Settings. WhatsApp permits catalog, inspect and activation commands, but
never remote package installation.

Firecrawl
---------

When Web Search is OFF, no Firecrawl process is started. With Web Search ON,
the first WebSearch/WebFetch request starts the bundled deployment through
rootless Podman. Its official container images are downloaded once into the
current user's Podman storage.

Useful diagnostics:

  gnomeai-firecrawl status
  gnomeai-firecrawl logs
  gnomeai-firecrawl stop

Podman is a recommended dependency because a remote Firecrawl URL can also be
configured instead. The local deployment binds only to 127.0.0.1:3002.

Provider account authentication
-------------------------------

OpenAI account authentication runs through the bundled official
`codex login --device-auth` flow. Anthropic account authentication requires
the official `claude` command; desktop launches also search the native install
locations under ~/.local/bin and ~/.claude/bin. Set GNOMEF_CLAUDE_BIN for a
custom path. Those account-backed modes are selected from the terminal agent.
WebTool uses API-backed providers, including the native Anthropic Messages API.

WhatsApp
--------

The package contains the pinned Baileys/Pino dependencies and depends on
Node.js 20 or newer; no runtime `npm install` is needed. Starting WhatsApp from
WebTool waits for the bridge and then displays the QR code automatically.
Startup and connection failures are shown in Settings and recorded under:

  ${XDG_STATE_HOME:-$HOME/.local/state}/gnomeai-rs/whatsapp_bridge.log
